00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.750 align:start position:0%
 
welcome everybody my name is clinton  jones and i believe the new year isn't a  new year without some growth it's a  chance for us to learn from last year so  we can challenge ourselves and grow this  year so i say we kick off 2022 with a  challenge  [Music]  i'm proud to announce the infinite  journeys 3d community challenge so  during the month of february i challenge  you whether you're new to 3d or not to  download the template 3d file in the  description and create the 3d scene that  you see in your head because in march  i'm piecing them all together so we can  create the chillest character based 3d  travel montage the internet has ever  laid eyes on you have one month to let  your passion run wild and put your  creativity to the test it doesn't matter  how much experience you have what  program you use or where you're from  this is for every 3d artist looking for  a fun challenge but before we get into  any details i am proud to announce an  amazing prize pool donated from  companies whose products i use and love  and they're all ready to be shipped to  any winning artist around the globe so i  know a lot of artists are trying to  learn unreal engine this year and even a  little bit of houdini so if your render  comes in fifth place mograph.com  is going to help you out with your  choice of any course on their site we're  talking a 40-hour houdini course a  20-hour unreal course by my good friend  winbush six hour procreate course for  you 2d enthusiasts and an ar workflow  lesson by none other than don allen  stevenson iii the guys at mograph.com  are awesome people and i am honored to  have them as part of the infinite  journeys challenge moving on to fourth  place a mograph.com course  that's yours plus  this incredible holographic display from  looking glass factory it's called the  looking glass portrait and it displays  your custom art and more in 3d no glass  is needed the looking glass supports  blender unreal engine and unity if  you're trying to export art specifically  for the looking glass you can even make  interactive experiences with this thing  and convert any photo for 3d display the  possibilities are endless with this  thing and i'm excited for you to see how  cool it is in person let me tell you  about third place though so the third  place artists get a looking glass too as  well as their choice of a monograph.com  course but also one of my all-time  favorite tools it keeps my bones healthy  and my art looking good and i'm talking  about a wacom intuos pro tablet in the  prize pool on behalf of the wonderful  people at wacom now a buddy of mine  bruce got me hooked on these tablets a  long time ago at first i was like i  don't know but if i'm gonna use a  computer for the rest of my life why not  be healthy about it now this wacom  intuos pro tablet is a must for any  artist working on a computer if risk  longevity isn't enough for you wacom is  letting you choose between a small  medium or large this one is a medium i  think it works perfect for my setup but  it's up to you depending on your setup  you can't go wrong  i'm going to take this to the grave  now if your 3d creation comes in second  place you're getting two extra things  actually on top of the mograph.com  course the looking glass portrait and a  wacom intuos pro tablet maxxon is  throwing in an annual max on one  subscription now that's complete with  cinema 4d of course redshift forger and  the entire red giant suite i've been  using cinema4d for nearly 10 years now  and i am honored to officially have  maxon join us as a sponsor this year and  i mentioned two things because our good  friends at rococo are throwing in a pair  of smart gloves for all the professional  level finger tracking you can get your  hands on now these babies are gonna save  lives when you're trying to animate all  this kind of stuff i can't wait to see  what kind of magic you come up with when  you get your hands on a pair of these  and the lucky artist who creates their  next masterpiece during the infinite  journeys 3d challenge  we'll receive the mograph.com course the  looking glass portrait a wacom intuos  pro tablet the maxon one annual  subscription the pair of smart gloves  and a full  performance capture bundle from the  beautiful people at rococo which ships  with not only the smart gloves and their  brand new smart suit pro 2 but a face  capture license and a face cap body  mount to make animation a blast  personally i can't wait to get my hands  on their new suit because they not only  improved its accuracy and performance  from the first version but added  elevation tracking unlocking a whole new  level of mocap options but that is not  all on behalf of the wonderful people at  camp mograph they are hooking you up  with an all-expenses paid trip to join  myself and an entire community of 3d  artists in silver beach virginia in  september for cambograff 2022 colbit  permitting campmograph is hands down the  greatest 3d artist meetup of all time  where a bunch of incredible 3d artists  step away from their computers and into  nature to hang out play games and learn  from each other for like five days  straight last year was my first time and  i had the honor of teaching a service  imperfection class and even a couple  yoga classes it was my favorite event of  last year and i wouldn't miss it for  anything this year so i'm excited to see  you there i want to give a very big  thank you to our sponsors maxon rococo  camp mograph wacom looking glass factory  and mograph.com for sponsoring infinite  journeys and keeping these prizes  available internationally it's very  important they stay international and  you guys really hooked it up so here's  how you join first download the project  file in the description inside we got a  blender file unreal engine c4d and an  fbx file the scene is the same  regardless of what program you're using  once you open up the project file you'll  be looking at a center framed window on  a wall which you're going to turn into  any mode of transportation that you want  that looks out to any setting you want  this challenge is simple because there's  only four simple rules rule number one  keep your mode of transportation moving  to the right so whatever's on the other  side of your window should be scrolling  to the left rule number two you must  capture the sense of movement it's not a  travel montage if we don't feel like  we're moving right rule number three you  gotta add at least one character between  the camera and the window because it's  gonna be boring without a subject and  rule number four  do not touch the camera this ensures  each render connects to the next via the  window as our universal focal point and  that's it the rest is up to you and how  far your creativity and passion will  take you this month and i know we're  going far together yo you all got this  now if you've done these community  challenges before you know it's a great  way to learn and grow no matter your  skill level or program of choice  so to the artists who want to get into  3d this is a perfect opportunity let's  jump in and for you veterans out there i  can't wait to see what you all whip up  the submission deadline is sunday  february 27th at 11 59 pm pst and a  submission link will be provided two  weeks into the challenge on february  12th i'll also announce the mystery  judge judges as we get further into  february and finally you know i'm not  going to leave you all hanging while you  create so to get started myself and the  create with clint discord moderators put  together a series of questions to help  you generate a unique idea for your 3d  scene as well as a short list of faqs to  keep you on the right track the server  is our home base during the infinite  journeys challenge and beyond because  it's full of passionate artists looking  to share their works and progress and  give out pointers to the artists who may  need them so be sure to hop in so you  don't miss important announcements or  updates and for the month of february i  will see each and every one of you every  single saturday as i live stream my  infinite journeys submission y'all i  can't wait to learn grow and create  through this challenge with everybody so  let's crush it and i'll see you guys at  10 45 am pst saturday the 5th so we can  work on this together now go get it  peace  [Music]  you

